--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-003-validate-the-complete-json-patch-document-before-evaluation.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+---
+id: dl-003-validate-the-complete-json-patch-document-before-evaluation
+type: decision-log
+title: "Validate the complete JSON Patch document before evaluation"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+RFC 6902 defines a JSON Patch as a JSON document whose top-level value is an array of operation
+objects. The operation evaluator previously validated only the operation members it used, allowing
+non-JSON values in ignored members and non-JSON JavaScript objects to be treated as patches.
+
+## Decision
+
+Validate the entire patch value as JSON before checking that its top-level value is an array and
+before applying operations. Continue to ignore additional operation members when their values are
+valid JSON, as required by RFC 6902.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Invalid patch input fails before evaluation. Valid extension members remain interoperable and do not
+affect operation semantics.
